The circumstances include: (SCC p. 286, para 28) "(i) The High Court's decision is based on totally erroneous view of law by ignoring the settled legal position;
(ii) The High Court's conclusions are contrary to evidence and documents on record;
(iii) The entire approach of the High Court in dealing with the evidence was patently illegal leading to grave miscarriage of justice;
State Of Gujarat Thro' B.N.Chaudhary vs Laxmanbhai Ranaji Patel-Owner & Vendor ... on 18 July, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/49147823/
